Database migrations (Alembic)
=============================

The schema is defined by the SQLAlchemy models in app/models/model.py and
applied to a database by Alembic migrations in alembic/versions/.

The DB URL is NOT configured here -- alembic/env.py reads it from the app
config (settings.DATABASE_URL), so migrations always target whatever
environment ENV_FILE points at. Run all commands from the backend/ directory
with the venv active.

Common commands
---------------
  alembic current                 # which revision the DB is at
  alembic history --verbose       # list all revisions
  alembic upgrade head            # apply everything up to latest
  alembic downgrade -1            # roll back one revision

Targeting an environment
------------------------
  alembic upgrade head                       # local (.env)
  ENV_FILE=.env.test alembic upgrade head     # Test
  ENV_FILE=.env.production alembic upgrade head  # Production

After changing a model
----------------------
  1. Edit app/models/model.py
  2. alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"
  3. OPEN the generated file in alembic/versions/ and check it -- autogenerate
     misses some changes (server-default changes, some constraint renames,
     enum value changes, data migrations) and can get column-type changes
     wrong. Adjust by hand as needed.
  4. Test it: `alembic upgrade head` then `alembic downgrade -1` on a
     throwaway database.
  5. Commit the migration file WITH the model change in the same commit.

Notes
-----
- env.py sets render_as_batch=True for SQLite so local dev can run ALTERs
  that SQLite doesn't support natively; it's a no-op on Postgres.
- ENV=local still auto-creates missing tables on `uvicorn main:app` startup so
  a fresh clone runs without a migrate step. Test / Production do NOT --
  `alembic upgrade head` is part of every deploy there (see docs/PROMOTION.md).
- alembic.ini's sqlalchemy.url is a placeholder only; env.py overrides it.
